I'm building a grid based rpg.

* Each heroes can bring up to 3 cards for a fight.

* Each turn they can move + use one of the cards (there's no drawing cards)

* Cards level up based on usage and can evolve when reaching certain level threshold

* The heroes have 1 main weapon card, and utility cards from their class

* Their class is based on their weapon evolution. They start with a basic club (=> hobo class).

* When reaching the evolution level they can choose their archetype (short sword => fighter, staff => mage, mace => cleric, dagger => rogue, bow => archer)

* Unlocking a class give a small stats boost and allow to choose one utility card from this class (example the fighter can choose the shield block card)

* The hobo class has the bandage utility card (a small self heal)

* higher tier classes can still access the lower tier utility cards they have unlock (meaning all classes have access to the bandage cards)

* the main weapon card is the primary damage dealer of the heroes, the utility cards are designed to not compete for damage. They can still do small damage, but they should be designed for "utility" (eg push pull, create obstable on the grid, summoning, buff/debuff)

***
Working gameplay systems:

Battle:
* grid movement
* card based combat
* card leveling and evolution
* class system based on weapon evolution
* class based utility cards
* class based stat bonuses
* class based passive bonuses
* LoS interception

World Map:
* node exploration
* battle on nodes which hand the predetermined encounters to the battle system.
